# B.3 Main Models: Englishness (Continuous) {#sec-b3-engl}

This section re-estimates the full set of meso-level models using Englishness rather than Britishness as the individual-level identity moderator. The exercise serves two purposes: assessing whether the conditional effects of local economic conditions are specific to state-level British identification, and enabling a theoretically meaningful comparison between Britishness and the sub-state Englishness identity within the same institutional context. Both identities are measured on identical 1–7 scales and harmonised using identical procedures; the empirical strategy — individual and wave FE, clustered SEs — is held constant throughout.

## B.3.1 Local Unemployment Rate {#sec-b3-unemp}

When Englishness replaces Britishness, local unemployment keeps exerting no statistically significant unconditional effect on immigration attitudes once individual and wave fixed effects are accounted for. Englishness itself is strongly and negatively associated with permissive immigration attitudes across all main-effects specifications. The interaction models, again, yield no evidence of meaningful conditional moderation: the interaction term between Englishness and unemployment is zero to three decimal places and entirely non-significant, and this null result is unchanged by the inclusion of age controls. The Englishness main effect remains stable and precisely estimated throughout.

```{r b3-unemp-main}
modelsummary(
  list(
    "(1) Unemp only"     = m_u0.1_eng,
    "(2) + Englishness"  = m_u1_eng,
    "(3) Unemp + Age"    = m_u0.2_eng,
    "(4) + Englishness"  = m_u2_eng
  ),
  coef_rename = c(
    engl            = "Englishness",
    unemployment_rate = "Unemp. rate (local)",
    age             = "Age"
  ),
  gof_map = GOF_MAP,
  stars   = c("*" = .05, "**" = .01, "***" = .001),
  title   = "Table B3.1. Local Unemployment Rate and Immigration Attitudes: Main Effects (Englishness)",
  notes   = "Individual and wave FE. SEs clustered by respondent. DV: immigSelf.",
  escape  = FALSE,
  output  = "kableExtra"
) |> kable_styling()
```

```{r b3-unemp-int}
modelsummary(
  list(
    "(1) Interaction"       = m_u3_eng,
    "(2) Interaction + Age" = m_u4_eng
  ),
  coef_rename = c(
    engl                        = "Englishness",
    unemployment_rate             = "Unemp. rate (local)",
    "engl:unemployment_rate"      = "Englishness × Unemp. rate",
    age                         = "Age"
  ),
  gof_map = GOF_MAP,
  stars   = c("*" = .05, "**" = .01, "***" = .001),
  title   = "Table B3.2. Local Unemployment Rate × Englishness: Interaction Models",
  notes   = "Individual and wave FE. SEs clustered by respondent. DV: immigSelf.",
  escape  = FALSE,
  output  = "kableExtra"
) |> kable_styling()
```

## B.3.2 Claimant Count {#sec-b3-claimant}

Claimant count results under Englishness present a more informative picture. Main-effect specifications again show no significant unconditional association between local claimant intensity and immigration attitudes. The interaction models, however, reveal a negative and statistically significant interaction between Englishness and claimant count (β ≈ −0.004, p \< 0.01), robust to the inclusion of age controls. This indicates that higher local claimant rates are associated with more restrictive immigration attitudes among respondents with weaker English identification, with the effect attenuating as Englishness increases. The claimant count main effect is positive but non-significant in these specifications.

```{r b3-claimant-main}
modelsummary(
  list(
    "(1) Claimant only"  = m_c0.1_eng,
    "(2) + Englishness"  = m_c1_eng,
    "(3) Claimant + Age" = m_c0.2_eng,
    "(4) + Englishness"  = m_c2_eng
  ),
  coef_rename = c(
    engl          = "Englishness",
    claimant_rate = "Claimant count (local)",
    age           = "Age"
  ),
  gof_map = GOF_MAP,
  stars   = c("*" = .05, "**" = .01, "***" = .001),
  title   = "Table B3.3. Claimant Count and Immigration Attitudes: Main Effects (Englishness)",
  notes   = "Individual and wave FE. SEs clustered by respondent. DV: immigSelf.",
  escape  = FALSE,
  output  = "kableExtra"
) |> kable_styling()
```

```{r b3-claimant-int}
modelsummary(
  list(
    "(1) Interaction"       = m_c3_eng,
    "(2) Interaction + Age" = m_c4_eng
  ),
  coef_rename = c(
    engl                   = "Englishness",
    claimant_rate          = "Claimant count (local)",
    "engl:claimant_rate"   = "Englishness × Claimant count",
    age                    = "Age"
  ),
  gof_map = GOF_MAP,
  stars   = c("*" = .05, "**" = .01, "***" = .001),
