  notes   = "Individual and wave FE. SEs clustered by respondent. DV: immigSelf.",
  escape  = FALSE,
  output  = "kableExtra"
) |> kable_styling()
```

## B.3.3 Local Income (ASHE) {#sec-b3-income}

Local income main-effect specifications show no significant unconditional association with immigration attitudes under Englishness, consistent with the Britishness results. The interaction models reveal a statistically significant conditional structure: the earnings main effect is positive and significant (p \< 0.01), while the Englishness × local income interaction is negative and significant (p \< 0.001), robust to age controls. Higher local earnings are therefore associated with more restrictive attitudes among respondents with weaker English identification, with this association attenuating as Englishness increases. The Englishness main effect in the interaction models is not significant, in contrast to the Britishness specifications where it was precisely estimated.

```{r b3-income-main}
modelsummary(
  list(
    "(1) Income only"   = m_i0.1_eng,
    "(2) + Englishness" = m_i1_eng,
    "(3) Income + Age"  = m_i0.2_eng,
    "(4) + Englishness" = m_i2_eng
  ),
  coef_rename = c(
    engl         = "Englishness",
    earnings_median  = "Local income (ASHE)",
    age          = "Age"
  ),
  gof_map = GOF_MAP,
  stars   = c("*" = .05, "**" = .01, "***" = .001),
  title   = "Table B3.5. Local Income (ASHE) and Immigration Attitudes: Main Effects (Englishness)",
  notes   = "Individual and wave FE. SEs clustered by respondent. DV: immigSelf.",
  escape  = FALSE,
  output  = "kableExtra"
) |> kable_styling()
```

```{r b3-income-int}
